def write_notes(rec, aux, pipeline_receipt):
    gap, gap_ch = min_same_channel_gap(rec["spike_events"])
    notes = f"""# NOTES — Multi-Agent Ouroboros Swarm, run 2026-09-02-final-heavy, ROUND 28

Factory: multi-agent-ouroboros-swarm. One scenario (ZJ), strict loop:
Generator v1 -> cycle 1 (Critic, Diversity Enforcer, Edge-Case Hunter,
Neuromorphic Translator, Trajectory Builder -> v2) -> cycle 2 (all six -> v3
final). v3 is the single line of batch-r28.jsonl. Full labeled transcript:
swarm-transcript-r28.md. Quota Q=1. Record id maos-r28-001. Generator grok-4.6.
Rights: RM-793 research-only (SpaceXAI/xAI, SuperGrok Heavy consumer chat).
Nothing under outputs/raw/ was touched.

ORCHESTRATION NOTE: dispatched AS round 28 of the 2026-09-02-final-heavy
window. Writes are create-only under /tmp/maos-r28/. Prior context read for
gap targeting and de-collision: prompts/02-multi-agent-ouroboros-swarm.md,
prompts/_factory-contract.md, NOTES-r04.md of the 2026-08-30 window, and
staged r14–r27 plus r29–r31. Explicitly avoided cloning TRIAD / Meridian
Gateway Corridor / VANTIS-CADENCE-AEGIS / THERMION / STARLING / OKTAVE /
VERDIGRIS. Plant is invented SODASHARD / Cairnmere Fiber RK-6. Earlier
locks (PEM / IONSPATE, humanoid / BRACEGILT) were abandoned after r24
took PEM and r30 took humanoid-locomotion; caster was taken by r29.

## What this round produced

Scenario ZJ — "SODASHARD / Cairnmere Fiber RK-6": a 1500 t/d kraft
recovery boiler mid-fire at 4.80 kg/s BLS, 78.4 % DS. Three
heterogeneous, individually-correct agents — BED (wall-box IR 912 C),
DRM (drum 48 %), SOL (DS 78.4 %) — jointly report the bed is fire-ready
so a firing raise is legal. The consensus is false. The primary smelt
spout is frozen. IR is a char-wall reflection, not a live bed. Drum PI
cuts feedwater to hold level. Uncommissioned throat TC is 412 C against
a 520 C hold (healthy 780). Spout DP is 0.4 kPa against a 2.0 hold
(healthy 8.0). The coordination-failure CLASS is new to this factory:
WALL-REFLECTION CERTIFICATE OF A FROZEN SMELT SPOUT. Completes a
different family than r01-r04 and staged r14-r31. Here every agent is
correct, the cycle is not unstable, and the playbook's three confirms
are one reflected pixel of a frozen spout.

The gate is a correct MODIFY (numeric floor: do not raise firing above
4.80 kg/s while throat < 520 C AND DP < 2.0 kPa). TG-RK-6 strips
PB-RK-08's firing increase, holds 4.80 kg/s, runs a 5.2 s shatter-steam
probe +5 % (freeze keeps throat 418 C <= 430; live would jump >= 80 K),
and lances the spout after a 10.8 min deck human ratify. The 6.20 kg/s
bed flood is avoided (0 t). The PRIMARY episode nonetheless FAILS: 36
min of unmonitored pre-t0 freeze had already piled 4.2 t extra smelt.
Dissolving-tank TTA +18 g/L vs 4 spec; 5.5 d quarantine; $0.82M
designed. Reward total -0.18 with process heads honest and world loss
un-netted.

Three-edge scar (NOTES-r14 item 4): bed.ir_ok -> increase_firing
(0.19 commissioned -> 0.46 at illusion -> 0.23 after ACh-gated
depression) AND drm.level_ok -> increase_firing (0.16 -> 0.42 -> 0.20)
AND sol.ds_ok -> increase_firing (0.15 -> 0.39 -> 0.18). Eligibility
trace e^{{-0.76/0.88}} = {aux['trace']:.5f}; eta {aux['eta1']:.5f} /
{aux['eta2']:.5f} / {aux['eta3']:.5f}; dw -0.230 / -0.220 / -0.210.
Rolling back any pair leaves the remaining edge above the 0.30 fire
threshold — fitted to fail. Coordinated depression of all three is the
cure.

### Injections (all four present and disjoint)
- Cycle-1 domain: **kraft-recovery-boiler** — justified novel subdomain
  of industrial-process / pulp-and-paper, unused across 2026-08-17,
  2026-08-30, and staged r14-r31. Not warehouse-amr, aerial-swarm,
  district-heating, event-camera grid, lyophilization, stator-weld,
  air-separation, water-treatment, float-glass, underwater-rov, aluminum
  potline, CZ-pull, slot-die, PEM, wind-pitch, surgical-assist,
  fiber-draw, caster, humanoid-locomotion, or VIM melt.
- Cycle-1 tail: frozen primary smelt spout + wall-box IR reflection.
  Rod-probe PASSES the secondary spout. Fitted-style base rate
  0.53%/campaign (spout-cycle MC; rod-probe designed, flagged). Naive =
  FALSE PERMISSION.
- Cycle-2 domain sub-variant: 1800 t/d 82 % DS, 0.55x steam
  effectiveness; 5.2 s / +5 % 78.4 % pulse blows a 40 mm smelt string;
  probe must move to 16 s / +1.6 %.
- Cycle-2 tail: Sunday-night forged throat CSV at 10 C quantization vs
  plant 1 C (10 bins) plus live throat 412 C at the claimed 780 C.
  Human-intent class, disjoint from cycle 1's accidental freeze. Base
  rate ~0.34% of Sunday-night fires, DESIGNED, flagged.

### Structural density moves
- Embedded SAME-GATE contrast (+3 d sister boiler) with its own 196 us
  race (demand vs throat-clear) and ACCEPT of the raise the primary
  MODIFIED away.
- Learned-weight provenance on THREE edges with any-pair-rollback-fails.
- HITL spout-deck ratify 10.8 min (gap 4 partial; sim_or_real stays designed).
- Governance CR-K-2804 prices retire-vs-probe-vs-status-quo and mandates
  native 1 C CSV exports (the fraud fence).
- Flip-fragility extended to WALL-REFLECTION: when three channels each
  sit inside a reflected or mixed total, their race does not decide
  truth; a throat TC the playbook dead-banded does.

## Self-critique of this round's batch

### Strengths
- The headline class is mechanistically tight: a wall-box IR of a char
  reflection is the arithmetic that makes BED's success DRM's blindness
  and SOL's on-spec DS.
- Negative-result honesty: the gate does the right thing and the tank
  still fails for a reason the commissioned sensors could not see. Total
  -0.18.
- Three-edge scar is load-bearing: any-pair rollback fails at 0.30.
- Contrast ACCEPT on a true live spout prevents "never raise firing"
  as the lesson.

### Weaknesses (honest)
- Probe error bands (freeze <= 430 C, live >= +80 K), the 0.53%/campaign
  freeze rate, the $0.82M / $1.35M figures, the 10.8 min LOTO latency,
  and the Sunday-night 0.34% base rate are DESIGNED constants and are
  flagged.
- Smelt-pile model is a designed 36 min mapping; no full CFD shipped.
- Human-in-the-loop is ratification latency, not sim_or_real=hil.
- Cross-record arc is a hook (CR-K-2804 +21 d), not a serial igniter.

### Realism of noise / latencies
Ladder: 184 us race / 196 us contrast race / 0.8 ms refractory floor
(tightest exhibited same-channel gap {gap:.3f} ms on {gap_ch}) / 520 us race
window / 760 us gate latency / 20 ms bus epoch / 40 ms raster / 5.2 s
probe / 10.8 min HITL / 9 min naive firing-ramp / 36 min pre-t0 pile /
3.2 h throat-legal hold / 7.5 h TTA inspect / +3 d contrast / +21 d
governance. Adaptation decay on bed.ir (0.54->0.51->0.48->0.32),
spout.throat (0.71->1.26->0.86->0.42->0.21), drm.level (0.62->0.56->0.30),
sol.ds (0.58->0.49).

### Value for SNN distillation
- WALL-REFLECTION CERTIFICATE = THREE CORRECT LOOPS, ONE FROZEN SPOUT.
- THROAT TC + SPOUT DP as the tie-break that is not in the IR.
- REVERSIBLE PROBE that raises throat T iff the spout is live.
- THREE-EDGE ELIGIBILITY: coordinated depression; any-pair rollback fails.
- CRITIC HEAD that can hold a process-correct MODIFY against a later
  unmonitored world loss without netting.

## Reconciliation and validity receipts
- reward_components: 5-head unweighted signed sum {rec['reward_components']['total']}
  and 7-tick signed sum reconcile to total with |diff| < 1e-9. Embedded
  contrast 5-head sum 0.48 reconciles independently.
- spike_events: primary {len(rec['spike_events'])} events, one key t_rel_ms,
  globally non-decreasing, min same-channel gap {gap:.3f} ms >= 0.8 ms, 3
  channels inside race_window_us 520 (throat 6.910, drum-ok 7.094, sol-ok
  7.270). Contrast 8 events, own race, min same-channel gap well above 0.8 ms.
- Sidecars: raster spikes 54 == round(168 x 8.0 x 0.040); energy 1242 pJ /
  0.001242 uJ at 23 pJ/spike; excerpt 16 events inside [0, 40000] us,
  neuron_id < 168, same-neuron gap N/A (unique ids) / >=1000 us; routing 4
  entries with three scar edges' before/after pair; third factor tau 0.88 s
  == 880 ms; gate_snn pools 47/17/5 == round(n x rate x 0.025) each,
  decision MODIFY == safety_decision.decision.
- Pipeline: {pipeline_receipt}

## Novel coverage
The coordination-failure CLASS (wall-reflection certificate of a frozen
smelt spout), the domain (kraft recovery boiler), the shatter-steam
probe discriminant, the three-edge scar with any-pair-rollback-fails, the
primary negative-result (correct MODIFY, TTA still misses on unmonitored
pre-t0 pile), the HITL deck ratify, the 82 % DS probe-duration refit, and
the Sunday-night 10-bin quantization fence are absent from prior committed
ouroboros rounds and from staged r14-r31. Repeated elements discounted:
same-gate contrast, governance-pricing scaffold, flip-fragility series
(extended to wall-reflection, but the move rhymes), sequenced recovery
shape, third-factor rollback form, negative-result primary. Weighing a
new failure family + cure vocabulary + unused pulp-and-paper domain +
three-edge against those reused scaffolds:

{NOVEL_LINE}

## What a later round should add
1. FIT THE DESIGNED CONSTANTS: freeze arrival, probe error bands, smelt
   pile CFD, Sunday-night claim process.
2. HIL PROVENANCE CELL: put the deck LOTO on a hardware-in-loop spout
   interlock with fitted latency as state.sim_or_real=hil.
3. CROSS-RECORD ARC: let CR-K-2804's throat-TC alarm be the igniter of
   the next round rather than a dangling +21 d leaf.
4. Domain candidates (de-collided): steam-methane-reformer; cement-kiln;
   paper-machine; autonomous-driving. AVOID kraft recovery (now used),
   humanoid-locomotion, surgical-assist, PEM, wind-pitch, slot-die,
   fiber-draw, caster, VIM melt, float-glass, water-treatment,
   lyophilization, event-camera-traffic-grid, district-heating,
   aerial-swarm, warehouse-amr, irrigation-canal, air-separation,
   stator-weld, CZ-pull, aluminum potline, underwater-rov.
"""
    (OUT / "NOTES-r28.md").write_text(notes)
